<?xml version="1.0"?>
<page xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
      xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:framework:View/Layout/etc/page_configuration.xsd">
    <body>
        <referenceBlock name="head.additional">
            <!--
                Deliberately on every page rather than only on pages holding a slider, and
                deliberately in the head. Two separate constraints happen to point the same way:

                * the import map must be installed before the first module script anywhere in the
                  document, and layout cannot know whether a CMS block three levels down contains a
                  slider widget;
                * `<script type="module">` is deferred by definition, and deferred scripts run in
                  document order — so an entry module rendered from `before.body.end` runs *after*
                  Hyvä's Alpine, which has already walked the DOM and found no `scr1beSlider`
                  registered. Moving this block there was tried and produced exactly that: a page
                  full of `scr1beSlider is not defined`.

                `before="-"` puts the map ahead of the mega menu's module tag, which is also written
                into this container. It is the only import map the storefront prints — Firefox
                installs the first one a document declares and rejects the rest, so the mega menu,
                the product card and the back-in-stock popup all import their siblings relatively
                and print none. The last of those kept a map until a second pass found it: rendered
                from its own `default.xml`, behind this block, it was never the one installed. This
                one stays because its engine specifier is a rebindable seam (see SliderScripts).
            -->
            <block class="Scr1be\HyvaProductSlider\Block\SliderScripts"
                   name="scr1be.slider.scripts"
                   before="-"
                   template="Scr1be_HyvaProductSlider::scripts.phtml"/>
        </referenceBlock>
    </body>
</page>
